    "question": "Charley has a bag that contains 51 white beads and 90 black beads. He reaches in the bag and pulls out 1/6 of the black beads and a third of the white beads. How many beads in total did Charley pull out?",
    "gold": "32",
    "answer": "Charley pulled out 90/6 = <<90/6=15>>15 black beads.\nCharley pulled out 51/3 = <<51/3=17>>17 white beads.\nCharley pulled out 15+17 = <<15+17=32>>32 beads in total.\n#### 32"
  },
  "generation": {
    "text": "To determine how many beads Charley pulled out, we need to calculate the number of black beads and white beads he pulled out separately and then sum them up.\n\nFirst, let's calculate the number of black beads Charley pulled out. The bag contains 90 black beads, and he pulls out \\(\\frac{1}{6}\\) of them:\n\\[\n\\frac{1}{6} \\times 90 = \\frac{90}{6} = 15\n\\]\nSo, Charley pulled out 15 black beads.\n\nNext, let's calculate the number of white beads Charley pulled out. The bag contains 51 white beads, and he pulls out \\(\\frac{1}{3}\\) of them:\n\\[\n\\frac{1}{3} \\times 51 = \\frac{51}{3} = 17\n\\]\nSo, Charley pulled out 17 white beads.\n\nNow, we add the number of black beads and white beads together to find the total number of beads Charley pulled out:\n\\[\n15 + 17 = 32\n\\]\nTherefore, the total number of beads Charley pulled out is \\(\\boxed{32}\\).",
